<concept base="Anywhere" id="t00476">
	<title>Emergency Steering (Driver steering assist)</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e03221">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03222">
								<image href="images/N_SP3i25_C00_017_IR.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e03223">
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Emergency Steering</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>Emergency Steering can alert you with Emergency steering warning light blinking (<image href="images/WKIA_077.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/>), a warning message, an audible warning and steering wheel vibration (if equipped).</p>
		<p>If there is a risk of a collision with another vehicle or a pedestrian, cyclist, or motorcyclist ahead of your vehicle, Emergency Steering can assist you in steering to help prevent a collision.</p>
		<p>Emergency steering will be activated in following conditions.</p>
		<p>Your driving speed: Approximately 40–85 km/h (25–53 mph)</p>
	</conbody>
